\f0\cf1\fs44\b Privacy Watch\b0\par
\cf2\fs24 A local history of your Mac's reported privacy activity.\par
\par
\fs28\b Install\b0\fs24\par
1. Drag Privacy Watch.app onto the Applications shortcut in this disk image. If updating, quit the running copy first.\par
2. Eject the Privacy Watch disk image. Open Privacy Watch from Applications. Do not run setup from the disk image.\par
3. Choose Set Up & Start Logging and approve the protected-log reader in the macOS administrator dialog.\par
4. Choose your sensors, log folder and notifications in Settings. Test a microphone or camera and confirm a fresh activity row.\par
\par
\fs28\b First-launch security message\b0\fs24\par
This free build is locally signed and is not notarized by Apple. If you trust this download and choose to open it:\par
1. Click Done in the Privacy Watch Not Opened warning to keep the app.\par
2. Open System Settings > Privacy & Security. Scroll the main pane on the right down to Security, near the bottom of the page.\par
3. Look for "Privacy Watch was blocked to protect your Mac." Click Open Anyway on the right of that message, just above FileVault. The exact layout can vary with your macOS version.\par
4. Confirm Open in the next dialog and use your password or Touch ID if macOS asks. Enter credentials only in the macOS dialog.\par
\par
Privacy Watch appears in a temporary blocked-app message, not in the Camera, Microphone or other app-permission lists. If the message is missing, open the installed app again, click Done, then return to this area of Settings. You do not need to add Full Disk Access or change Allow applications from.\par
\par
BlockBlock users may see a separate non-notarized-process alert. Review the app name and path and choose Allow only if you intend to run that copy. BlockBlock may ask again after reboot. Some managed Macs prohibit exceptions. Keep Gatekeeper and BlockBlock enabled.\par
\par
\fs28\b Requirements and startup\b0\fs24\par
Targets macOS 14 or later, with Apple Silicon and Intel binaries. Runtime testing was on Apple Silicon/macOS 27; other versions and Intel execution remain unverified. An administrator is required for protected-reader setup. Each Mac needs its own approval.\par
\par
To start after sign-in, add Privacy Watch under System Settings > General > Login Items & Extensions > Open at Login. Keep Start logging automatically when the app opens enabled in Privacy Watch settings.\par
\par
\fs28\b Documentation and source\b0\fs24\par
The Documentation folder includes setup, privacy, troubleshooting, uninstall and license information. No personal history is included in this download.\par
